{%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
  <style>
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
      {%- unless section.settings.allow_transparent_header -%}
        margin-block-start: calc(var(--section-vertical-spacing) / 2);
      {%- endunless -%}
      --slideshow-top-gap: {% unless section.settings.allow_transparent_header %}calc(var(--section-vertical-spacing) / 2){% else %}0px{% endunless %};
      margin-block-end: var(--section-vertical-spacing);
      {%- if section.settings.transition_type != 'fade' -%}
        --slideshow-background: {{ section.settings.background.rgb }};
      {%- endif -%}
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    First section on the page, right under the site header: the gap above the slideshow is the page's side margin (--container-gutter), the same as every
    other first section (theme.css), instead of half of the section spacing. The min-height below subtracts the same value (--slideshow-top-gap), so the slideshow
    still fills the screen. With the transparent header there is no gap and nothing changes.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- unless section.settings.allow_transparent_header -%}
      main > #shopify-section-{{ section.id }}:first-child {
        margin-block-start: var(--container-gutter);
        --slideshow-top-gap: var(--container-gutter);
      }
    {%- endunless -%}

    {%- if section.settings.floating_slideshow -%}
      {%- comment -%}
      The page's side gutter (the .container margin) sits on the section wrapper itself, outside the section, instead of on the
      slideshow inside it: the editor's outline then spans only the slideshow, which still respects the page's side padding.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
        margin-inline: max(var(--container-gutter), 50% - var(--container-max-width) / 2);
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow-wrapper {
        margin-inline: 0;
      }
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.border_radius == 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
      theme.css gives .slideshow a mask-image, a trick to make overflow: hidden follow rounded corners in Safari. With square corners it
      does nothing visible, but a mask forces the browser to composite and repaint the whole slideshow, videos included, on every frame -
      a known cause of choppy video. Only kept when the corners are rounded.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow {
        -webkit-mask-image: none;
        mask-image: none;
      }
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.hide_header_logo -%}
      {%- comment -%}
      "Hide the header logo": the logo in the header is hidden only while the header is transparent (over this slideshow, before scrolling).
      Once the header turns solid (scrolled, or a menu / search / cart drawer open) the logo comes back, with the same timing as the header's
      own text and logo swap; scrolling back to the top hides it again. It is only made invisible and unclickable - not removed - so the
      header's layout (menu centering, icons) stays where it is and screen readers still get the store name.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      .header__logo {
        transition: opacity var(--header-solid-transition, .45s cubic-bezier(.4, 0, .2, 1)) var(--header-content-delay, 0s);
      }

      .header:not(.is-solid, :has([open])) .header__logo {
        opacity: 0;
        pointer-events: none;
      }
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.blur_intensity > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
      Blur only (the same backdrop blur the pop-ups and the newsletter use), with no color: a layer over each IMAGE slide's picture (video slides are left alone),
      under the text, so the text stays sharp. It covers the whole slide and never blocks clicks or swipes.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__blur {
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        grid-area: auto;
        -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur({{ section.settings.blur_intensity }}px);
        backdrop-filter: blur({{ section.settings.blur_intensity }}px);
        pointer-events: none;
      }
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
    Logo on an image slide (snippets/slideshow-logo.liquid), over the picture and under the slide's text. Its box is absolutely positioned: it
    fills the slide but takes no part in the slide's layout, so the image's own size can never widen the slide. grid-area: auto matters: the
    content box gives every direct child the grid-area of its inner area (theme.css), and an absolute child of a grid is sized against its
    grid area. The box has NO padding: the logo goes right to the edge of the picture - to the top edge, the bottom edge or the middle (the
    slide's "Logo position" setting) - and, in full size, from side to side. Whatever the picture's rounded corners or the slide's edge cut
    off is simply cut. Never blocks clicks or swipes.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      grid-area: auto;
      box-sizing: border-box;
      padding: 0;
      pointer-events: none;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      overflow: hidden;
      display: flex;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo--top {
      align-items: flex-start;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo--bottom {
      align-items: flex-end;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo img {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      width: min(var(--slideshow-logo-width), 100%);
      height: auto;
      max-width: none;
      max-height: none;
      min-width: 0;
      min-height: 0;
      object-fit: contain;
      backface-visibility: hidden;
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo img {
        width: min(var(--slideshow-logo-width-desktop), 100%);
      }
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    Full size (after the rules above, so it wins on mobile and desktop alike): the logo spreads from one side of the slide to the other, with no
    margin, and its height follows from its own proportions. It is sized by the width on purpose: the slide's height moves by a few pixels while the
    page is scrolled (the sticky header and the announcement bar change the space the slideshow is measured against), and a logo sized by that
    height grew and shrank with it. Sized by the width it stays the same.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo--full img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    The text's distance from the slide's edges is the same inner padding as the floating containers (container gutter + 0.5rem,
    see faq.liquid / reviews.liquid), at every width. .content-box
    (theme.css) is shared with many other sections, so its own value (the larger of 1.5rem and the gutter, shrinking
    in narrow containers) stays as is and is only overridden here; the section id in the selector beats those
    container-width rules.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__slide .content-box {
      --content-box-spacing: calc(var(--container-gutter) + 0.5rem);
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    A heading with its decorative icon is a full-width row (title on one side, the icon on the other), so inside a
    centered or end-aligned slide the title would stay at the start while the rest of the text follows the slide.
    Shrinking the row to its content lets the prose rules (margin-inline: auto on its children) place it like any
    other text block.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__slide .prose > .heading-icon-row {
      width: fit-content;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
    Matches the existing .min-h-fill convention (assets/theme.css): subtract the sticky header/
    announcement bar area from the svh height, since that's real occupied space above the fold on
    every page except when this section is both first AND allows a transparent header - there, the
    header floats over the slideshow instead of pushing it down, so only the (non-transparent)
    announcement bar/countdown still needs subtracting. A bar that is not sticky is not part of the sticky area, so the room it takes
    (--announcement-bar-space, header.liquid) is subtracted on its own.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__slide .content-box {
      min-height: calc({{ section.settings.mobile_height }}svh - var(--sticky-area-height, 0px) - var(--slideshow-top-gap, 0px) - (1 - var(--announcement-bar-is-sticky, 0)) * var(--announcement-bar-space, 0px));
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }}:first-child [allow-transparent-header] .slideshow__slide .content-box {
      min-height: calc({{ section.settings.mobile_height }}svh - var(--announcement-bar-height, 0px) - var(--announcement-bar-gap, 0px) - var(--header-top-gap-rest, var(--header-top-gap, 0px)) - var(--countdown-condensed-height, 0px));
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__slide .content-box {
        min-height: calc({{ section.settings.desktop_height }}svh - var(--sticky-area-height, 0px) - var(--slideshow-top-gap, 0px) - (1 - var(--announcement-bar-is-sticky, 0)) * var(--announcement-bar-space, 0px));
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }}:first-child [allow-transparent-header] .slideshow__slide .content-box {
        min-height: calc({{ section.settings.desktop_height }}svh - var(--announcement-bar-height, 0px) - var(--announcement-bar-gap, 0px) - var(--header-top-gap-rest, var(--header-top-gap, 0px)) - var(--countdown-condensed-height, 0px));
      }
    }

    {%- if section.settings.logo_scroll_effect == 'fly' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
      "Logo scroll effect: Fly to the header" (driven by <slideshow-logo-flight> below). While the effect runs, the root carries:
      - data-logo-fly: the effect is on. The header's own logo is hidden until the flying logo reaches it.
      - data-logo-arrived: the slide's logo has reached the header logo: the two cross-fade in place (same spot, same size).
      - data-logo-flight: the logo is still on its way (or just arrived): the header stays on screen even if "hide on scroll" would slide it away,
        so the logo always has somewhere to land. Released a little after the arrival; hide on scroll then works as usual.
      Visitors who prefer reduced motion get no flight: the header logo is just hidden while the header is transparent (same as "Hide the header logo").
      {%- endcomment -%}
      :root[data-logo-fly] .header__logo {
        transition: opacity .35s ease;
      }

      :root[data-logo-fly]:not([data-logo-arrived]) .header__logo {
        opacity: 0;
        pointer-events: none;
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo img {
        transform-origin: center;
        transition: opacity .35s ease;
      }

      :root[data-logo-arrived] #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .slideshow__logo img {
        opacity: 0;
      }

      :root[data-logo-flight] .shopify-section--header,
      :root[data-logo-flight] .shopify-section--header .header {
        transform: none !important;
        visibility: visible !important;
      }

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .header:not(.is-solid, :has([open])) .header__logo {
          opacity: 0;
          pointer-events: none;
        }
      }
    {%- endif -%}
  </style>

  <div class="slideshow-wrapper {% if section.settings.floating_slideshow %}container{% endif %}">
    <slideshow-carousel id="slideshow-{{ section.id }}" allow-swipe cell-selector=".slideshow__slide" {% if section.settings.allow_transparent_header %}allow-transparent-header{% endif %} class="slideshow" transition="{{ section.settings.transition_type }}" {% if section.settings.autoplay %}autoplay="{{ section.settings.cycle_speed }}" {% if section.settings.pause_auto_rotate_on_hover %}pause-on-hover{% endif %}{% endif %} style="border-radius: {{ section.settings.border_radius }}px;" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.slideshow' | t | escape }}">
      {%- content_for 'blocks' -%}

      {%- if section.blocks.size > 1 -%}
        {%- content_for 'block', type: '_slideshow-controls', id: 'slideshow-controls' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </slideshow-carousel>
  </div>

  {%- if section.settings.logo_scroll_effect == 'fly' -%}
    <slideshow-logo-flight section-id="{{ section.id }}" hidden></slideshow-logo-flight>

    <script>
      {%- comment -%}
      Fly to the header: while the page scrolls, the logo of the slideshow travels to the exact spot of the logo in the header, shrinking to its
      size, tied to the scroll (half way down, half way there; scrolling back up brings it back, growing again). It flies over the transparent
      header; when it lands the header turns solid (the #header-scroll-tracker of layout/theme.liquid, which sets .is-solid, is moved to the landing distance, so the
      header's own paint transition starts exactly then) and the two logos cross-fade in place.

      The distance of the flight is the vertical distance between the two logos at the top of the page (D). The logo already rises with the page at
      the scroll speed, so it reaches the header's height after exactly D pixels of scroll: on the way only a small vertical correction is needed
      (the header can move a little - the announcement bar scrolls away, the header padding changes), plus the sideways move and the shrink.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      if (!window.customElements.get('slideshow-logo-flight')) {
        window.customElements.define('slideshow-logo-flight', class extends HTMLElement {
          connectedCallback() {
            if (window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;

            this.section = document.getElementById('shopify-section-' + this.getAttribute('section-id'));
            this.tracker = document.getElementById('header-scroll-tracker');
            this.root = document.documentElement;

            // Only when the header is transparent over this slideshow: the slideshow is the first section of the page and allows it
            var firstSection = document.querySelector('main > .shopify-section');
            if (!this.section || firstSection !== this.section || !this.section.querySelector('[allow-transparent-header]')) return;

            this.abort = new AbortController();
            var options = { signal: this.abort.signal, passive: true };
            this.update = this.update.bind(this);
            this.requestUpdate = function () {
              if (this.frame) return;
              this.frame = requestAnimationFrame(function () { this.frame = null; this.update(); }.bind(this));
            }.bind(this);

            window.addEventListener('scroll', this.requestUpdate, options);
            window.addEventListener('resize', function () { this.measured = false; this.requestUpdate(); }.bind(this), options);
            window.addEventListener('load', function () { this.measured = false; this.requestUpdate(); }.bind(this), options);
            document.fonts && document.fonts.ready.then(function () { this.measured = false; this.requestUpdate(); }.bind(this));

            // Theme editor: changing a header setting (eg. its layout, logo on the left or in the center) re-renders the header, and the logo
            // element measured before is thrown away. Everything is measured again from the new header (update() also checks it on every frame).
            ['shopify:section:load', 'shopify:section:unload', 'shopify:section:reorder'].forEach(function (type) {
              document.addEventListener(type, function () { this.measured = false; requestAnimationFrame(this.requestUpdate); }.bind(this), { signal: this.abort.signal });
            }.bind(this));

            this.root.setAttribute('data-logo-fly', '');
            this.update();
          }

          disconnectedCallback() {
            if (this.abort) this.abort.abort();
            if (this.frame) cancelAnimationFrame(this.frame);
            this.root && ['data-logo-fly', 'data-logo-arrived', 'data-logo-flight'].forEach(function (name) { this.root.removeAttribute(name); }.bind(this));
            if (this.tracker) this.tracker.style.top = '0px';
            if (this.logo) this.logo.style.transform = '';
          }

          // The logo of the slide on screen (the first one with a logo when no slide is marked as selected)
          findLogo() {
            return this.section.querySelector('.is-selected .slideshow__logo img, [aria-current="true"] .slideshow__logo img') || this.section.querySelector('.slideshow__logo img');
          }

          findTarget() {
            return document.querySelector('.header__logo-image:not(.header__logo-image--transparent)') || document.querySelector('.header__logo');
          }

          // Where the slide's logo sits in the page without any flight (its own transform taken off for the measure), and the flight distance
          measure() {
            var logo = this.findLogo();
            var target = this.findTarget();
            if (this.logo && this.logo !== logo) this.logo.style.transform = '';
            this.logo = logo;
            this.target = target;
            if (!logo || !target) return false;

            var transform = logo.style.transform;
            logo.style.transform = 'none';
            var rect = logo.getBoundingClientRect();
            logo.style.transform = transform;

            this.start = {
              x: rect.left + rect.width / 2 + window.scrollX,
              y: rect.top + rect.height / 2 + window.scrollY,
              width: rect.width
            };

            // The header's logo at the top of the page: its position now, minus how far the header has moved since (it is sticky, so it
            // does not move with the scroll once stuck - at the top of the page both are the same)
            var targetRect = target.getBoundingClientRect();
            var targetY = window.scrollY < 1 ? targetRect.top + targetRect.height / 2 : (this.targetY0 || targetRect.top + targetRect.height / 2);
            this.targetY0 = targetY;

            this.distance = Math.max(0, this.start.y - targetY);
            if (this.tracker) this.tracker.style.top = Math.round(this.distance) + 'px';
            this.measured = this.distance > 0 && rect.width > 0;
            return this.measured;
          }

          update() {
            // The header logo (or the slide's logo) was replaced (header re-rendered, layout or logo changed): measure the new one
            if (this.measured && (!this.target.isConnected || !this.logo.isConnected)) this.measured = false;
            if (!this.measured && !this.measure()) return;

            var scroll = window.scrollY;
            var progress = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, scroll / this.distance));
            var targetRect = this.target.getBoundingClientRect();
            var targetX = targetRect.left + targetRect.width / 2;
            var targetY = targetRect.top + targetRect.height / 2;

            // Where the logo is without any transform (it rises with the page), and where it should be at this point of the flight
            var naturalX = this.start.x - window.scrollX;
            var naturalY = this.start.y - scroll;
            var x = naturalX + (targetX - naturalX) * progress;
            var y = progress < 1 ? naturalY + (targetY - naturalY) * progress * progress : targetY;
            var scale = 1 + (targetRect.width / this.start.width - 1) * progress;

            this.logo.style.transform = 'translate3d(' + (x - naturalX) + 'px, ' + (y - naturalY) + 'px, 0) scale(' + scale + ')';

            this.root.toggleAttribute('data-logo-arrived', progress >= 1);
            this.root.toggleAttribute('data-logo-flight', scroll < this.distance + 200);
          }
        });
      }
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.slideshow.name",
  "class": "shopify-section--slideshow",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 5,
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": [
      "header",
      "custom.overlay"
    ]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "allow_transparent_header",
      "label": "t:global.section.allow_transparent_header",
      "info": "t:global.section.allow_transparent_header_info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "floating_slideshow",
      "label": "Floating",
      "info": "Activado: el slideshow respeta los márgenes laterales de la página y el marco del editor se ajusta solo a él. Desactivado: va de borde a borde de la pantalla.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_radius",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.border_radius",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "blur_intensity",
      "label": "Blur (image slides)",
      "info": "Blurs the picture of every image slide, without adding any color. The text stays sharp. Video slides are not blurred. 0 turns it off.",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 10
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Header logo"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "hide_header_logo",
      "label": "Hide the header logo",
      "info": "Hides the logo at the top of the header while the header is transparent over this slideshow. It shows again once the header turns solid on scroll.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "logo_scroll_effect",
      "label": "Logo scroll effect",
      "info": "Fly to the header: on scroll, the logo of the slide shrinks and travels to the logo of the header, then the header turns solid. Use the same logo design in the slide and in the header. Works when this slideshow is the first section, with the transparent header.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "None" },
        { "value": "fly", "label": "Fly to the header" }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "mobile_height",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.mobile_height",
      "min": 30,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "desktop_height",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.desktop_height",
      "min": 30,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "transition_type",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "fade",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.fade"
        },
        {
          "value": "vertical_reveal",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.vertical_reveal"
        },
        {
          "value": "curtain",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.curtain"
        },
        {
          "value": "distortion",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.distortion"
        },
        {
          "value": "perspective",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.perspective"
        },
        {
          "value": "scale_down",
          "label": "t:sections.slideshow.transition_type_options.scale_down"
        }
      ],
      "default": "curtain"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "autoplay",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.auto_rotate_between_slides",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "pause_auto_rotate_on_hover",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.pause_auto_rotate_on_hover",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.autoplay }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "cycle_speed",
      "min": 4,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "sec",
      "label": "t:sections.slideshow.cycle_speed",
      "default": 6,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.autoplay }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background",
      "label": "t:global.colors.background",
      "info": "t:sections.slideshow.background_info",
      "default": "#000000"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_slideshow-image-slide"
    },
    {
      "type": "_slideshow-video-slide"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:sections.slideshow.name",
      "category": "t:global.categories.banners",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "_slideshow-controls",
          "id": "slideshow-controls",
          "static": true
        },
        {
          "type": "_slideshow-image-slide",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "settings": {
                "text": "Slide 1",
                "heading_size": "h1"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "_slideshow-image-slide",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "settings": {
                "text": "Slide 2",
                "heading_size": "h1"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
